  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C. Line 2 oven trays with baking paper. Peel the carrot, then cut the carrot and zucchini into 1.5cm-thick batons.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/255385/photos/large/prep_ingredients-acd5165f1f5771a6e19742db9106b1b2.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep crumbing mixture: Whisk 2 eggs and 1 tsp dijon mustard in a shallow bowl. Put 1 tbs plain flour on a plate, then season with salt and pepper. Combine the breadcrumbs and country seasoning on a separate plate.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/255386/photos/large/prep_crumbing_mixture-cf296fe3f7318d283bb534ca56c1300f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Crumb zucchini: Dust the zucchini in the flour, shaking off the excess. Dip in the egg mixture, then coat in the seasoned breadcrumbs. Put on a lined tray. Put the carrot and sausages on the remaining lined tray, ensuring the sausages don't touch as they may stick together during cooking. Drizzle with 2 tsp olive oil, then season the carrot with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/255387/photos/large/crumb_zucchini-5cffbd1ae38e9e5ac7b10ddbeffc8a90.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast veg and sausages: Roast the zucchini fries on the upper oven shelf and the carrot and sausages on the lower shelf for 18-20 mins until golden and tender.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/255388/photos/large/roast_veg_and_sausages-b4e9b8a2212af8fccad5ae72cc458c0f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Meanwhile, bring a medium saucepan of salted water to the boil. Add the broccolini and cook for 2 mins or until tender. Drain, then season with salt and pepper. Divide the sausages, roasted veggies and broccolini among plates and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/255389/photos/large/serve_up-99153d3cc79840a60dafa984e880826f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: Like things saucy? Serve the vego sausages with your favourite dipping partner – whether it's mayonnaise, tomato relish or trusty barbecue sauce.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/255390/photos/large/make_it_yours-64b077cee496991e83b043cdf9de1a3d.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
